theory MKA_Basic

begin

/*

=============================================================
MKA (MACsec Key Agreement) Protocol Model
=========================================

This model represents a simplified version of IEEE 802.1X MKA.

Included functionality:

* Shared CAK assumption
* Derivation of ICK and KEK
* Peer discovery
* Key Server election
* Secure Association Key (SAK) generation
* Secure SAK distribution
* Key confirmation

Excluded functionality:

* SCI handling
* Priority-based election
* Live Peer List
* Rekey procedure
* SAK rollover
* Multiple participants

The purpose of this model is to verify:

* Authentication
* SAK secrecy
* Key confirmation

*/

builtins: hashing

functions:

```
kdf_ick/1,
kdf_kek/1,

mac/2,

senc/2,
sdec/2,

basic/3,
dsak/2
```

equations:

```
sdec(senc(x,k),k) = x
```

/* ==========================================================
Long-term CAK installation
========================================================== */

rule InstallCAK:

```
[ Fr(~cak) ]
```

--[ CAKCreated(A,~cak) ]->

```
[ !CAK(A,~cak) ]
```

/* ==========================================================
Derive ICK and KEK
========================================================== */

rule DeriveKeys:

```
[ !CAK(A,cak) ]
```

--[ KeysDerived(A) ]->

```
[ !ICK(A,kdf_ick(cak)),
  !KEK(A,kdf_kek(cak))
]
```

/* ==========================================================
MKA Peer Discovery
========================================================== */

rule SendBasicParameterSet:

```
[ !ICK(A,ick),
  Fr(~mi),
  Fr(~mn)
]
```

--[ SendBasic(A,~mi,~mn) ]->

```
[ Out(
      <
        basic(~mi,~mn,A),
        mac(basic(~mi,~mn,A),ick)
      >
  )
]
```

rule ReceiveBasicParameterSet:

```
[ In(
      <
        basic(mi,mn,A),
        mac(basic(mi,mn,A),ick)
      >
  ),

  !ICK(B,ick)
]
```

--[ PeerAuthenticated(A,B) ]->

```
[ Peer(B,A) ]
```

/* ==========================================================
Key Server Election
========================================================== */

rule BecomeKeyServer:

```
[ Peer(A,B) ]
```

--[ KeyServer(A) ]->

```
[ KeyServerState(A) ]
```

/* ==========================================================
SAK Generation
========================================================== */

rule GenerateSAK:

```
[ KeyServerState(A),
  Fr(~sak)
]
```

--[ SAKGenerated(A,~sak) ]->

```
[ CurrentSAK(A,~sak) ]
```

/* ==========================================================
SAK Distribution
========================================================== */

rule SendSAK:

```
[ CurrentSAK(A,sak),
  !KEK(A,kek),
  !ICK(A,ick),
  Fr(~ki)
]
```

--[ SendSAK(A,sak) ]->

```
[ Out(
      <
        dsak(~ki,senc(sak,kek)),
        mac(dsak(~ki,senc(sak,kek)),ick)
      >
  )
]
```

rule ReceiveSAK:

```
[ In(
      <
        dsak(ki,senc(sak,kek)),
        mac(dsak(ki,senc(sak,kek)),ick)
      >
  ),

  !KEK(B,kek),
  !ICK(B,ick)
]
```

--[ ReceiveSAK(B,sak) ]->

```
[ InstalledSAK(B,sak) ]
```

/* ==========================================================
Key Confirmation
========================================================== */

rule SendConfirmation:

```
[ InstalledSAK(B,sak),
  !ICK(B,ick)
]
```

--[ ConfirmationSent(B,sak) ]->

```
[ Out(mac(sak,ick)) ]
```

rule VerifyConfirmation:

```
[ In(mac(sak,ick)),
  CurrentSAK(A,sak),
  !ICK(A,ick)
]
```

--[ SessionEstablished(A,sak) ]->

```
[ SecureChannel(A,sak) ]
```

/* ==========================================================
Compromise Model
========================================================== */

rule RevealCAK:

```
[ !CAK(A,cak) ]
```

--[ CAKReveal(A) ]->

```
[ Out(cak) ]
```

/* ==========================================================
Security Lemmas
========================================================== */

/*
Authentication:

If B receives a SAK,
some participant must have distributed it.
*/

lemma authentication:

"
All B K #i.

ReceiveSAK(B,K) @ i

==>

Ex A #j.

SendSAK(A,K) @ j
"

/*
Key confirmation:

If A establishes a secure session,
someone must have received the same SAK.
*/

lemma key_confirmation:

"
All A K #i.

SessionEstablished(A,K) @ i

==>

Ex B #j.

ReceiveSAK(B,K) @ j
"

/*
SAK secrecy:

An attacker cannot learn SAK
unless a CAK compromise occurred.
*/

lemma sak_secrecy:

"
All A K #i.

SessionEstablished(A,K) @ i

==>

(
not(Ex #j. K(K) @ j)
|

Ex B #r.
CAKReveal(B) @ r
)
"

end
